# Manim render output. Regenerable via:
#   $MANIM -qh animations/bob_overview.py BOBOverview
# Kept out of git so rendered video never bloats the clone permanently.
media/

# Video. The rendered masters under media/ stay out (they are regenerable and
# each re-render is another full copy), but the four DEPLOYED explainers in
# assets/ are tracked -- the site references them and GitHub Pages has to
# serve something.
#
# Those are web derivatives, not the masters: 30 fps, CRF 26, which is ~66%
# smaller than manim's 1080p60 output and visually identical on slide content
# (RMS difference 1.09/255 on the densest frame). Re-encode with:
#   ffmpeg -i media/videos/<scene>/1080p60/<Scene>.mp4 \
#          -c:v libx264 -crf 26 -preset slow -r 30 \
#          -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart -an assets/<name>.mp4
*.mp4
!assets/*.mp4

# Reference PDFs used while building the animations. Not site content, and
# several are other authors' published papers -- redistributing publisher
# PDFs from a personal domain is a copyright question worth avoiding.
# Nothing on the site links here; the animations cite arXiv numbers instead.
papers/

# One-off exploration scenes: grids of candidate background/accent colours,
# rendered as stills to pick a palette by eye. bg_swatches.py alone is 32
# throwaway Scene classes (BgCyanVivid, BgWVUGoldDeep, ...). They served
# their purpose -- the chosen values now live in the overview scripts -- and
# nothing references them. Kept on disk, out of the repo.
animations/bg_swatches.py
animations/bi_swatches.py

# Photo originals: phone shots and full-resolution press files, 1-4 MB each.
# Same discipline as the video masters -- tools/mkphotos.py emits small 3:4
# crops into assets/, and those ARE tracked because the site fetches them.
# Two of the originals here are (c) Institute for Advanced Study; keeping the
# folder out of git also keeps those out of the repo's permanent history.
anuj_photos/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Windows "downloaded from the internet" markers next to the papers
*:Zone.Identifier

# CV work. Two designs ship: cv/design-4-scan (the CV in use) and
# cv/design-10-newspaper (the broadsheet the nav links to). Everything else
# is exploration and stays out of history.
cv/other_design/
cv/_probe/

# Rendered CV output and the agents' working files. cv.html is the source,
# cv.pdf is the deliverable the site links, NOTES.md is the rationale --
# everything else in these directories is scratch: page rasters, greyscale
# proofs, zoom crops, .part fragments, one-off probes. Allowlisted rather than
# pattern-matched, because each design left a different mess and a pattern
# list silently misses the next one. Rasters regenerate in one command:
#   pdftoppm -png -r 110 cv/<dir>/cv.pdf cv/<dir>/page
cv/design-4-scan/*
!cv/design-4-scan/cv.html
!cv/design-4-scan/cv.pdf
!cv/design-4-scan/NOTES.md
cv/design-10-newspaper/*
!cv/design-10-newspaper/cv.html
!cv/design-10-newspaper/cv.pdf
!cv/design-10-newspaper/NOTES.md

# Typeface exploration: seven copies of the same markup in different font
# pairings, plus the iframe harnesses used to measure the nav breakpoint, prove
# each pooled typeface really loads, and drive the geodesic legend through its
# states. Useful on disk, not site content -- and the set-*.html pages fetch
# Google Fonts for families the site does not ship, which is exactly what the
# no-runtime-fetch rule forbids. Regenerate with tools/mktypetests.py.
type-tests/
tools/mktypetests.py

# Cartoon of the site owner drawn in the hero figure's idiom. Nothing links it.
anuj.png
anuj.svg
mkanuj.py

# Working notes. Kept on disk, out of the repo -- it is a scratch list of what
# is half-done and what is wrong with the site, which is useful to whoever is
# editing and not something to publish next to the site it describes.
# NOTE: untracking it does not remove it from history. It was committed in
# c80ef20 and three commits after, so the old copies remain recoverable from
# the log by anyone who clones. Rewriting history is the only way to change
# that, and it has not been done.
TODO.md
